			<div class="content" id="post-content-2149604">
									

<p>I'd assume that the Foundation would keep tabs on local criminal activity to detect potential anomalies, and when they noticed the denizens of a town performing some really bizarre ritualistic dance routine involving porcupines on the same day that a guy attempted to smuggle a bunch of porcupines (unless I'm mistaken, this doesn't seem like a normal occurrence), they at least suspected something was up. Afterwards they probably conducted a series of mild and controlled tests on the guy to see what the effects on the city were, and only then did they conclude that there was a definite correlation between the two.<br />
It's probably Euclid because there's no telling how the people of the town would react to certain situations. If the guy lead a terrorist attack, would the Foundation have a townful of possibly anomalously augmented people plotting acts of terrorism? If he died, would the entire town fall down dead? It's unpredictable, hence it's Euclid.</p>

