														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2150542">
									

<p>It's quite possibly just that it's being used as &quot;smash in a bunch of extra info that would otherwise break tone.&quot; Your thing is a rock what extracts people's souls? Have the article explain about prolonged contact deadening emotional responses, then link to a footnote: &quot;See also: 'Soul Removal and Links to Higher Brain Functions: On the Effects of SCP-XXXX&quot;. It's a cheat.</p>
<p>Now maybe they aren't <em>all</em> used like that, but I've quickly grown to discount them the moment I see them because they have been. I also think they're being overused quite a lot; I could see one, maybe two in a medium-length article, but some have upwards of five, for crying out loud.</p>

